msgstr "Humanity built a civilization where industrial and military mechs were in everyday use. The anomalous energy discovered later provided more output than existing fuels and was quickly adopted for power plants, new-model mech power and weapons. The early Frames that ran on electricity and oil were pushed aside as inefficient, outdated equipment.\n\nThe first signs of the anomaly appeared in animals around energy facilities. Their build and skeletons changed, their tissue gained new properties, and some animals began gathering where the energy had accumulated. The change, which began at industrial sites and habitats, spread through soil, water and the food chain.\n\nWhen monster attacks brought down power plants and production facilities, the fuel and parts supply chains that kept the new-model mechs running were also cut off. Humans abandoned the cities and scattered into small outposts. Where civilization vanished, new animals made their habitats.\n\nToday's monsters are living creatures that each eat, move, fight over territory and breed. Some mutant species already live on across generations and form food chains with the ordinary plants and animals that survived. Conflicts arise because the roads and facilities humans used overlap with their territories."

